{"uid":"drivers/usbhid.c::usbhid_set1_from_usage","name":"usbhid_set1_from_usage","qualname":"usbhid_set1_from_usage","kind":"function","file":"drivers/usbhid.c","line":117,"end_line":123,"language":"c","signature":"int usbhid_set1_from_usage(unsigned usage, unsigned char *sc, int *e0)","params":[{"name":"usage","annotation":"unsigned","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"sc","annotation":"unsigned char *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"e0","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"int","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Docstring: Translate a HID usage code to its PS/2 set-1 make code and whether it needs the 0xE0 prefix.","description":"Returns 0 for a usage with no set-1 equivalent, which the caller drops rather than inventing a scancode for.\n\nA pure function over a table, host-testable: HID usage ids are not\nscancodes above 0x27 (usage 0x28 is Return while set-1 Return is 0x1C), and\nthe navigation cluster and the right-hand modifiers exist in one place on\na USB keyboard while set-1 needs the prefix to tell them from their\nleft-hand twins. Both decisions live here so no caller has to know them.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `usbhid_set1_from_usage` (headers/drivers/usbhid.h:127)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"drivers/usbhid.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"drivers/usbhid.c::USBHID_MAX_SCANCODES","name":"USBHID_MAX_SCANCODES","qualname":"USBHID_MAX_SCANCODES","kind":"macro","file":"drivers/usbhid.c","line":204,"end_line":239,"language":"c","signature":"#define USBHID_MAX_SCANCODES","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Docstring: How many scancodes a keyboard report transition can produce at worst: six keys each able to emit prefix plus make or break plus prefix break, plus eight modifier bits.","description":"Sized so the buffer is never the limit.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"drivers/usbhid.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"drivers/usbhid.c::usbhid_kbd_scancodes","name":"usbhid_kbd_scancodes","qualname":"usbhid_kbd_scancodes","kind":"function","file":"drivers/usbhid.c","line":206,"end_line":239,"language":"c","signature":"int usbhid_kbd_scancodes(const unsigned char prev[HID_KBD_REPORT_LEN], const unsigned char cur[HID_KBD_REPORT_LEN], unsigned char *out, int max)","params":[{"name":"HID_KBD_REPORT_LEN","annotation":"unsigned char prev[ ]","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"HID_KBD_REPORT_LEN","annotation":"unsigned char cur[ ]","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"out","annotation":"unsigned char *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"max","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"int","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Docstring: Set-1 scancode stream for one keyboard report transition.","description":"Pure: no hardware, no kernel state, no allocation, which is what makes it\nhost-testable. Breaks are emitted before makes, for modifiers and for keys\nalike, so a burst never reads as a held-key repeat. A key that merely moved\nslot within the array produces nothing, because the array order is the\ndevice's choice. Returns the number of scancodes written, which is less\nthan max only when the report produced no events.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `usbhid_kbd_scancodes` (headers/drivers/usbhid.h:94)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"drivers/usbhid.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":["headers/drivers/usbhid.h::HID_MODIFIER_BIT"],"called_by":["drivers/usbhid.c::usbhid_press_kbd_report"]}
{"uid":"drivers/usbhid.c::usbhid_mouse_decode","name":"usbhid_mouse_decode","qualname":"usbhid_mouse_decode","kind":"function","file":"drivers/usbhid.c","line":241,"end_line":254,"language":"c","signature":"void usbhid_mouse_decode(const unsigned char prev[HID_MOUSE_REPORT_LEN], const unsigned char cur[HID_MOUSE_REPORT_LEN], int *dx, int *dy, int *buttons, int *wheel)","params":[{"name":"HID_MOUSE_REPORT_LEN","annotation":"unsigned char prev[ ]","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"HID_MOUSE_REPORT_LEN","annotation":"unsigned char cur[ ]","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"dx","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"dy","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"buttons","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"wheel","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"void","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Docstring: Decode one boot mouse report transition into screen-space motion, buttons and wheel.","description":"Pure, for the same reason. dx and dy are raw report deltas; the caller applies the motion scale, matching the PS/2 path so both sources move the pointer identically.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `usbhid_mouse_decode` (headers/drivers/usbhid.h:102)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"drivers/usbhid.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
